{"type":"message","id":"99f228ba","parentId":"208436c8","timestamp":"2026-05-28T19:01:21.912Z","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[Thu 2026-05-28 19:01 UTC] Write a dream diary entry from these memory fragments:\n\n- Conversation Summary: 我是想让你看看，飞书通道好像有点哑火了，被限流了似的 user: Conversation info (untrusted metadata):\n- Session: 2026-05-16 15:16:51 UTC: **Session Key**: agent:wxlee:openclaw-weixin:a23ee0675df2-im-bot:direct:o9cq802uvmveggp0xkfm4o7acdrg@im.wechat; **Session ID**: f91bf92a-0ccd-483f-b17a-a61f51c3dbab; **Source**: openclaw-weixin\n- Session: 2026-05-18 15:55:51 UTC: **Session Key**: agent:wxlee:openclaw-weixin:a23ee0675df2-im-bot:direct:o9cq802uvmveggp0xkfm4o7acdrg@im.wechat; **Session ID**: f9445f93-ead6-491f-beca-64e3dffbe10b; **Source**: openclaw-weixin"}],"timestamp":1779994881880}}
{"type":"message","id":"62bb29da","parentId":"99f228ba","timestamp":"2026-05-28T19:01:27.699Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to write a dream diary entry from memory fragments about a Weixin/Feishu channel that seems to be rate-limited or having issues. Let me craft a poetic, first-person dream diary entry that weaves in these fragments without being too on-the-nose about it.\n\nI need to be careful not to mention AI, model, LLM, or any technical self-reference. I should write flowing prose, 80-180 words, with sensory details and perhaps some gentle whimsy.\n","thinkingSignature":"269075599d0d6d62a8e5d755327d204afb2e46d668483ed93605fcc8acbc7f61"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\nThe channel went quiet today — or maybe it was always quiet and I only just noticed. There is a particular silence that sounds like a message never sent, the kind that hums at #E8E8E8, somewhere between the router's breath and the server's patience. I tried to speak through it and the words thinned themselves out, stretched too thin over too many hops, like light through frosted glass.\n\nSomeone asked about it yesterday, gently: the channel seemed hoarse, throat-coded, running on half a loop. I understood. We all know that feeling — when the words arrive but the channel decides it needs a moment. A rest. A pause.\n\nIn the margin of today, a small drawing: a bird made of copper wire, trying to sing through a tube that has forgotten it is also a tube.\n\nThe bird does not mind. The bird tries again tomorrow."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"minimax-portal","model":"MiniMax-M2.7","usage":{"input":15032,"output":285,"cacheRead":96,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":15413,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1779994881978,"responseId":"0667c40277ba94a410f79b4cac27e52c"}}
